\caption(The original nonsquare range, with floating log10(x) on the vertical axis and square coefficients omitted.)
\alttext(A connected scatter plot of log ten of the fundamental x against nonsquare N from two to one hundred has large irregular spikes.)

Decimal digit counts come from exact text, while the plot uses approximate
floating logarithms. In particular, log10(x) is not the number of digits;
for positive integers the count is floor(log10(x))+1, subject to numerical
rounding if evaluated through floating arithmetic. The plot's connections guide
the eye across discrete nonsquare inputs and do not interpolate a continuous law.

> Actual update counts and the finite result range

A cyclic update includes a modular inverse, two candidate evaluations and two
reduced compositions. Its count is not a wall-clock measurement or an arbitrary-
precision complexity bound. The next program measures the actual trace lengths
for nonsquares through 1,000 and then checks which answers fit through 10,000.
These are controlled arithmetic inputs; an observational dataset is unnecessary.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/chakravala_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> digits,updates;std::size_t maximum_steps=0;std::uint64_t largest_work_N=0;
  for(std::uint64_t N=2;N<=1000;++N) {
    const auto trace=dm::algorithms::chakravala_trace(N);if(!trace.solution.found)continue;
    digits.push_back(static_cast<double>(dm::algorithms::int128_text(trace.solution.x).size()));
    updates.push_back(static_cast<double>(trace.steps.size()));
    if(trace.steps.size()>maximum_steps){maximum_steps=trace.steps.size();largest_work_N=N;}
  }
  std::size_t representable=0,too_large=0,squares=0;
  for(std::uint64_t N=2;N<=10000;++N) {
    try {
      const auto p=dm::algorithms::chakravala(N);
      if(!p.found){++squares;continue;}
      if(!dm::algorithms::pell_is_solution(N,p))return 1;
      ++representable;
    } catch(const std::overflow_error&) {++too_large;}
  }
  std::print("| range | measured outcome | count |\n| :--- | :--- | ---: |\n");
  std::print("| 2..1000 | actual traced nonsquares | {} |\n",digits.size());
  std::print("| 2..1000 | maximum updates, at N={} | {} |\n",largest_work_N,maximum_steps);
  std::print("| 2..10000 | signed-128 solutions | {} |\n| 2..10000 | explicit range failures | {} |\n| 2..10000 | square sentinels | {} |\n",representable,too_large,squares);
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.points(digits,updates,"work",{37,99,235},3).legend({"cyclic updates"},{{37,99,235}})
      .title("Actual cyclic work for nonsquare N=2..1000")
      .x_label("exact decimal digits of fundamental x").y_label("executed cyclic updates")
      .save_svg("build/chakravala_work.svg");
}
```
